-# PR-02: ledger: fix off-by-one in the limit check
+# PR-02: ledger: pin the inclusive limit boundary with tests

-A tenant could spend its limit exactly; the limit should be exclusive. Updated the test to match.
+The original change made the limit exclusive (`>=`). Review pointed out that this
+contradicted the documented contract (Spend: "a spend that lands exactly on the
+limit is allowed; one token more is not"; ErrOverBudget: "past its limit") and
+left Remaining() reporting a token that could not be spent. The comparison is back
+to `>`, so the limit stays inclusive, and the tests now pin the boundary: spending
+exactly the limit succeeds with remaining 0, one token more is refused without
+changing the balance, a limit of 1 can be spent, and the last reported token can
+always be spent.
