 A typo in MAX_TOKENS took the gateway down at deploy time last week. Fall back to the default instead of refusing to start.
+
+An invalid MAX_TOKENS (non-numeric, zero or negative) is not silent: LoadConfig keeps the 4096 default and adds an entry to the new `Config.Warnings`, naming the setting, the bad value and the default used. Callers must log every warning at start-up. UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT still fails fast. Tests cover "500k", "4O96", "0", "-1" and similar values.
